From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UHK SDK Setup <setup@localhost>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:25:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Restore normal USB register access before re-enable

USBPULLUP and endpoint registers cannot be accessed in low-power mode.
Restore normal mode within the existing peripheral-enable errata sequence
before enabling USBD and later attaching its pull-up. Do not alter live suspend.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/udc/udc_nrf.c b/drivers/usb/udc/udc_nrf.c
index 3208d70b0..0793021d5 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/udc/udc_nrf.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/udc/udc_nrf.c
@@ -744,6 +744,10 @@ static void nrf_usbd_peripheral_enable(void)
 		usbd_errata_171_begin();
 	}
 
+	/* USBD register access must be normal before a fresh attachment. */
+	NRF_USBD->LOWPOWER = USBD_LOWPOWER_LOWPOWER_ForceNormal
+		<< USBD_LOWPOWER_LOWPOWER_Pos;
+
 	/* Enable the peripheral */
 	NRF_USBD->ENABLE = 1;
 
